10 different conditions for class "0" (Does NOT read academic books most of the time):
- Reason for reading books is in [Entertainment Purpose, To increase my English vocabulary knowledge, Keep me informative]
- Department is in [English, BBA, JMC, Others]
- Favorite books for reading to spend leisure time is in [Fiction, Biography, Others]
- Frequency of reading books is in [A few times a month, Rarely, Once a week]
- Amount of time spent reading books per day < 1
- Number of e-books you read last two years is in [nan, 1-5]
- Number of printed books you read last two years is in [nan, 1-5]
- What is the change that you felt after reading books is not "Increase Academic Performance"
- Who influenced you to read books is in [Friends, Family, Self-motivation]
- How to manage books for reading is in [Buy, Used-all, Others]

10 different conditions for class "1" (Reads academic books most of the time):
- Reason for reading books is Academic Purpose
- Department is in [CSE, SWE, Pharmacy, EEE, Civil, Textile, CIS, MCT]
- Frequency of reading books is in [On everyday basis, Almost every day]
- Amount of time spent reading books per day >= 1
- Number of e-books you read last two years is in [6-10, 11-15, 16-20, More than 20]
- Number of printed books you read last two years is in [6-10, 11-15, 16-20, More than 20]
- What is the change that you felt after reading books is Increase Academic Performance
- Who influenced you to read books is Teachers
- The format that you used for reading books is E-books
- Which language books do you like to read is in [English, Bangla]

---

These conditions capture the tendencies and patterns that distinguish students who read academic books most of the time (class 1) from those who do not (class 0).